-- title:
--   Functorial nilpotent-point criterion for ideal membership in B[[X]]
-- statement:
--   Let $B$ be a Noetherian commutative ring, let $\sigma$ be a finite type of variables, let $S$ be a set of multivariate power series in $B[[X_i : i \in \sigma]]$ and let $G$ be a further such power series. Here a power series $\varphi$ is evaluated at a tuple $a : \sigma \to C$ over a commutative $B$-algebra $C$ with a cut-off $n$ by [`MvFormalGroup.nilEval n φ a`](def/AlgebraicGeometry_FormalGroupAlongSection.html#L15), namely by forming the truncation of $\varphi$ to those monomials all of whose exponents are at most $n$ and applying the $B$-algebra evaluation of that polynomial at $a$. Assume that for every commutative $B$-algebra $C$ (in the ground universe), every ideal $J \subseteq C$, every $n \in \mathbb{N}$ with $J^{n+1} = 0$, and every tuple $s : \sigma \to C$ with $s_i \in J$ for all $i$, the vanishing $\mathrm{nilEval}\, n\, \varphi\, s = 0$ for all $\varphi \in S$ forces $\mathrm{nilEval}\, n\, G\, s = 0$. Then $G$ lies in the ideal of $B[[X_i : i \in \sigma]]$ generated by $S$.
--
--   This is the ideal-membership criterion which converts a functorial statement about vanishing at all tuples of nilpotents in $B$-algebras into an algebraic containment in the power series ring; it rests on the Noetherianity of $B[[X_i : i \in \sigma]]$ (cited here as [`MvPowerSeries.isNoetherianRing_of_finite`](thm.html#MvPowerSeries.isNoetherianRing_of_finite)) and on the resulting closedness of ideals for the adic topology. It is used repeatedly in the Čerednik–Drinfel'd formal $\mathcal{O}_D$-module material, for instance when producing and comparing homomorphisms of formal modules from their effect on points with nilpotent coordinates.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_MvFormalGroup_mem_span_of_forall_nilEval_eq_zero.lean

